  },
  "item-count": 1,
  "schema-version": 2,
  "sections": {
    "releases": [
      {
        "changes": [
          {
            "category": "added",
            "id": "added",
            "notes": "- Sample validation: series, value, and timestamp are checked at the single point of entry, rejecting with a named offending field rather than admitting a partially valid sample.\n- Injectable clock and env-read config, so rollup window width, per-series sample cap, and retention are both configurable per deploy and fully testable without the wall clock.\n- Bounded ingest queue between the wire and the store. On overflow it drops the oldest buffered sample and keeps the newest, incrementing a `dropped` counter so the loss is observable (see the \"Drop the oldest sample on ingest queue overflow\" decision).\n- In-memory per-series sample store: one timestamp-ordered, capacity-bounded bucket per series, with range queries and retention-based pruning.\n- Aligned fixed-width window rollups and a per-series summary (count, mean, min, max) over a trailing span, with gaps left as gaps rather than zero-filled.\n- Transport-agnostic router wiring ingest, series listing, and per-series summary onto the store, queue, and clock."
          }
